# The core's pull-request checks that need no secret, as one job (#376): the copy of the core (core-manifest.md), which
# fails a change whose core/ is not the core, whole, at the commit the manifest pins, or whose calls to the core's
# workflows are pinned where they differ from the core's at that pin; then, as steps of the same job, the copies,
# pointer, reading-size, workflow, entry-file, manifest and shape checks, with this project's config (checks/copies.json)
# and marks (checks/sizes.json); the description check ("Each PR has the headings" in core/roles/shared/work-flow.md),
# on a pull request that is no draft and not Dependabot's, so its types take in an edited description, which is checked
# again by itself; and the package check, where the starter kit wrote one (npm's signatures, or NuGet's restore), last.
# One job bills one runner's minutes where four or five did. On every pull request and push to main, docs-only changes
# included; in a private repository, as the starter kit writes it, on a pull request only once it is no draft
# (core/scripts/init.mjs, READY_ONLY). Read-only, and no secrets: the description reaches the core's script as data.
# A session may run the same steps by hand: node core/scripts/checks.mjs.
name: core

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, edited, reopened, synchronize, ready_for_review]

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  core:
    uses: {{core}}/.github/workflows/core.yml@{{pin}}
    with:
      copies: checks/copies.json
      sizes: checks/sizes.json
      description: true
